The scenarios of Test 81's change, as tests/test_toy_wire_stream.c printed them:
  courses with the stream's timer: 7 in Toy Commander, 3 in another title at its own table
  the stream's timer by the title's own table: taken in another title with both free, the second where the first is the title's, none without an admitted table, at another vector base, behind the title's own handlers, behind another default, or with both in use; the title's entries, priorities and its timers' reload, count and control as they were after each, and an entry or a priority the title took meanwhile left to it
  a title that takes the stream's timer while the stream runs, by its entry, by starting it, or under a wait that stands armed: never armed, stopped or answered by the stream again, the entry left to the title or given back to it, the waits ended as without a timer

